Skills demonstrated: reverse image search, visual feature analysis, source corroboration, structured identification of a subject from a single photograph.

Summary:
The challenge provides a single photograph of an unidentified armored military vehicle and asks five questions about it: vehicle type, manufacturer, service-entry year, country of origin, and passenger capacity. 
Reverse image search plus corroboration against manufacturer and encyclopedic sources identifies it as the Thales Bushmaster Protected Mobility Vehicle (PMV). The remaining attributes follow from the confirmed model.
Challenge description: "An anonymous source has shared a photograph of an unidentified military armored vehicle during field operations. Your mission is to conduct a comprehensive OSINT analysis to identify this vehicle and its specifications."

Approach:
The portal has three pages: Dashboard (scenario and objective), Evidence (the photograph plus initial observations), and Challenge (the five questions).
Record visual features first. From the image: a wheeled (4×4), high-hulled, armored personnel vehicle with a V-shaped hull profile, in a flat, open field near what appears to be a military installation.
Reverse image search. Upload the photo to TinEye, Google Images, and Yandex. Matches lead to official defense-force social-media posts of the same vehicle.
Confirm the model against the manufacturer's site and encyclopedic references, then read the specifications from those confirmed sources rather than from the image alone.

Findings:
Identified vehicle: Bushmaster Protected Mobility Vehicle (PMV), the New Zealand Defence Force variant.
